<< /A << /BBox [ 81.5244 483.194 513.354 761.443 ] /O /Layout >> /Alt (Sankey diagram showing profile stability between Grade 3 and 6. Students in the above average profile in Grade 3 had 70&percnt; change to be classified in the same profile in Grade 6 and 20&percnt; change to be classified in the average profile. Students in the two average profiles in Grade 3 had around 40&percnt; change to be classified in the same profile in Grade 6 and around 30&percnt; change to be classified in the other average profile or the above average profile. Students in the below average profile in Grade had 26&percnt; change to be classified in the same profile in Grade 6 and had 20 to 40&percnt; change to be classified in one of the average profiles. Other transitions were less common \(10&percnt; change or less\).) /K 40 /Lang (en-EN) /P 349 0 R /Pg 234 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
